## Migration: EventProcessor to .NET 8

### Problems in the Original Code

| API | Issue on .NET 8 |
|-----|-----------------|
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` (SYSLIB0006) |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Obsolete (SYSLIB0046 in .NET 9), unreliable on `WaitOne` |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` | Not cancellation-aware |
| Race condition | Multiple `Enqueue` calls between `WaitOne`/`Reset` lose signals |

### Patterns Identified

1. **Cancellable work loop** → `CancellationToken` checked in loop
2. **Blocking call interruption** → `WaitHandle.WaitAny` with `token.WaitHandle`

---

### Migrated Code

```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;

public class EventProcessor : IDisposable
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();
    private Task? _processTask;

    public void Start()
    {
        _processTask = Task.Run(() => RunLoopAsync(_cts.Token));
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken token)
    {
        try
        {
            await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(token))
            {
                Handle(item);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException) when (token.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // Normal shutdown — swallow at top-level orchestration point
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        _channel.Writer.TryWrite(item);
    }

    public async Task StopAsync(TimeSpan? timeout = null)
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete();

        // Give the loop time to drain, then force-cancel
        using var timeoutCts = new CancellationTokenSource(timeout ?? TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

        try
        {
            if (_processTask is not null)
                await _processTask.WaitAsync(timeoutCts.Token);
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            // Drain didn't finish in time — force cancel
            _cts.Cancel();
            if (_processTask is not null)
                await _processTask.ConfigureAwait(ConfigureAwaitOptions.SuppressThrowing);
        }
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _cts.Cancel();
        _cts.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item) { /* your logic */ }
}
```

